# Pairs with the assumption on E: the entry check. The WAL admits a stamped
# append from any loaded entry, without comparing the stamp with it. After a
# purge that finished on 10.2.0 the WAL-side floor is not raised, so the claim
# the re-created incarnation's first initialisation makes is the only fence on
# the purged incarnation's generation, and without the check a straddler of L's
# own shard root is allocated above the recorded close. The assumption is
# load-bearing.
MODULE: StraddlerBelowInitNoEntryCheck
TARGET: StraddlerBelowInit
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the WAL admits a stamped append below its loaded generation entry
PERTURBS: Alloc

--- FIND
    /\ UNCHANGED <<recreated, legacy, restarted, mInit, closedAt, markNew, caught, dup>>

Alloc(i) ==
    /\ UNCHANGED rd
    /\ pend[i]
    /\ next < MaxOff
    /\ loaded[i] # Unloaded
    /\ pstamp[i] >= loaded[i]
--- REPLACE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<recreated, legacy, restarted, mInit, closedAt, markNew, caught, dup>>

Alloc(i) ==
    /\ UNCHANGED rd
    /\ pend[i]
    /\ next < MaxOff
    /\ loaded[i] # Unloaded
\* MUTATION: the stamp is not compared with the loaded entry.
--- END
